## 7. Phase-by-Phase Build Plan

Mapped session-for-session to the Coding Shuttle Razorpay Clone cohort schedule.

| Session(s) | Cohort topic | FlashMart equivalent | State |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Orientation | Repo setup, base Spring Boot app per service, docker-compose skeleton | Not started |
| 2 | Gateway internals & diagrams | Architecture + purchase-flow sequence diagrams | Partly stale (§9) |
| 3 | Requirement gathering | `docs/requirements.md` | Needs a Revision-3 pass |
| 4 | Schema design | All five schemas + ERDs | **Design done**; ERDs need regenerating |
| 5–6 | JPA entities Part 1 & 2 | Entities + repositories: `FlashSale → FlashSaleItem → StockReservation`, `Order → OrderItem → Refund`, Identity and Notification entities | **Next** |
| 7–8 | Merchant API — signup, API key | Identity Service: brand + buyer signup/login, brand API key generation, `BrandUpserted` / `UserUpserted` outbox rows | |
| 9 | Order APIs with MapStruct | Order creation/status/list APIs, multi-item request/response, DTO↔entity mapping | |
| 10 | Payment Initiate API, Strategy | Reserve endpoint + Order's per-item loop, all-or-nothing, contractual evaluation order | |
| 11 | State Machine, Payment Adapter | Order state machine as **CAS writes**, not an enum field; payment adapter interface | |
| 12 | Vault Service, Card Payment | **Out of scope** — FlashMart stores no card data by design; the buyer pays entirely on the gateway's side. Stated explicitly in `docs/requirements.md` §8 | Resolved |
| 13 | Spring Security, Banking Simulator | JWT auth for buyers and brands; Banking Simulator reused for payment failure injection | |
| 14 | API Key Authentication | API-key auth for brand-facing endpoints (`key_hash` lookup) | |
| 15 | Redis caching, basic rate limiting | ⚠ Catalog read caching + buy-endpoint limiting — carried forward, **not yet designed** | |
| 16 | Rate Limiting, Idempotency | Idempotent order creation, initiate, and reserve — all three already have their DB constraints designed | |
| 17 | Transactions, Locking, Outbox | Locking on `available_stock`, isolation level decision, outbox tables in Order + Identity | |
| 18 | Outbox with Kafka | Outbox → Kafka relays; `PaymentConfirmed`, `OrderCancelled`, `BrandUpserted`, `UserUpserted`; idempotent consumers | |
| 19–20 | Webhooks with Retry | Inbound signed payment webhook + one-payment invariant; **refund worker** (claim lease + fence token); **reconciliation sweep**. Outbound brand webhooks — dropped, no replacement; see `docs/decisions.md` | |
| 21 | Settlement Engine | **N/A** — permanently out of scope | Removed |
| 22 | Distributed microservices setup | Four services behind the API Gateway, `/internal/**` unexposed | |
| 13–15 *(parallel track — runs alongside 13–15 above, not after 22; listed last only because this table is otherwise chronological)* | Advanced microservices, Kafka, Docker | Kafka backbone, Eureka discovery, Dockerized deployment | |

Sequencing note: the sweeps and the refund worker (sessions 19–20) are what make the design's
correction paths real. Until they exist, the design's guarantees are structural, not
operational.

