## 8. Load Testing & Success Metrics

**Targets to capture and document. None is claimed as achieved until measured.** These
correspond to the `NFR-P*` targets in `docs/requirements.md`.

| Metric | Target |
|---|---|
| Overselling incidents | Zero, under 5,000 concurrent buy requests against 500-unit stock for a single flash-sale item |
| p99 latency (buy endpoint) | Documented under peak simulated load (target < 500 ms), including the per-item reservation loop |
| Payment idempotency | Zero duplicate charges under simulated client retry storms |
| Reserve idempotency | A retried reserve after a Feign timeout never holds stock twice, and never loses stock |
| Post-deadline retry safety | A reserve retry arriving after the sale's `end_time` returns the existing reservation rather than failing the order |
| Circuit breaker behaviour | Fail-fast + `PAYMENT_UNAVAILABLE` when the gateway is forced down |
| CAS race resolution | Expiry sweep vs. arriving webhook: exactly one wins, the loser observes zero rows affected |
| One-payment invariant | A duplicate captured payment always produces exactly one `refunds` row |
| Reconciliation sweep | A payment whose webhook is dropped entirely is still found and refunded |
| Reservation release correctness | Every `OrderCancelled` reason releases every reservation for that order |
| Multi-item compensation | A mid-loop item failure releases every already-reserved item in that order |
| Outbox reliability | No lost events when a service is killed between the DB commit and the Kafka publish |
| Contact-cache ordering | An out-of-order `BrandUpserted` / `UserUpserted` never overwrites newer data |

**Tooling:** JMeter or Gatling for load; Grafana/Prometheus (optional stretch) for live metrics.

