## 11. Draft Resume Bullet Points

**To be finalized with real measured numbers — every `[X]` is a placeholder, not a claim.**

- Designed and built FlashMart, flash-sale infrastructure for brands on Spring Boot
  microservices (Order, Inventory, Identity, Notification), handling `[X]` concurrent purchase
  requests with zero overselling via optimistic concurrency control `[+ locking strategy, once
  decided]`.
- Implemented saga-based multi-item order orchestration with asynchronous compensation, making
  one service the sole authority on order state via compare-and-set writes — races between the
  expiry sweep, the payment webhook, and the request thread resolve on a single row.
- Enforced an "exactly one payment per order" invariant across an unreliable webhook boundary,
  with two independent producers of refund work: the webhook handler and a reconciliation
  sweep that queries the gateway by a deterministic idempotency key.
- Made every write path retry-safe — order creation, payment initiation, and stock reservation
  — using database-enforced idempotency keys, and every Kafka consumer idempotent under
  at-least-once delivery.
- Applied the transactional outbox pattern in two services plus a command-outbox table for
  refunds, so no business change can commit without its event or command.
- Integrated an external payment gateway via OpenFeign with Resilience4j circuit breakers and
  idempotency-key propagation, with `[X]` duplicate charges under simulated retry storms.
- Load-tested the purchase flow with JMeter/Gatling, achieving p99 latency of `[X]` ms under
  `[X]` concurrent users while maintaining stock consistency.

